* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window (issue #38, Part of #16)
* Schmitt-readout hysteresis, measured on the DUT's OWN schmitt_hv instance
* (XSCH) in isolation: a quasi-static triangular ramp on the integrating-node
* voltage, up then down, so the rising and falling trip points are separated
* by real state memory rather than by DC-sweep solution continuation.
*
* Why this deck exists separately from the block transient. `schmitt_hv` is
* the only element in lock_detector that has hysteresis at all, so V_TH+ and
* V_TH- are the block's hysteresis *mechanism*, in volts on VWIN. Row 16's
* criterion is stated in PHASE ERROR ("hysteresis >= 25% of window"), and the
* map from volts-on-VWIN to phase error runs through the integrating node's
* own dynamics. Measuring the mechanism here and the phase-error thresholds
* in tb_lock_ladder.sp.tmpl lets ../records/RECORD-001 say WHY the
* phase-error hysteresis comes out the way it does, instead of only that it
* does.
*
* A 2 us ramp is ~1700x slower than the integrating node's own measured RC
* (see ../corners/rc_extract.csv), so the trip points read here are
* quasi-static; the deck is cheap enough to run at every corner point rather
* than at a subset.
*
* NOTE ON POLARITY (see ../records/RECORD-001 Finding 1): schmitt_hv is an
* INVERTING Schmitt trigger, and in this design its output IS the block's
* LOCK pin -- there is no output inverter after it. So "OUT falls" is the
* rising input trip point. The measurement below is written in terms of the
* input voltage at which OUT crosses mid-rail, in each ramp direction, which
* is polarity-neutral.
*
* Substituted by ../testbench/run.sh: @CORNER_MOS@, @TEMP@, @VSUP@, @VMID@,
* @DUT@, @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (resolved filesystem path -- ngspice's
* `.lib`/`.include` parser does not expand shell/OS environment variables,
* issue #54).

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib res_typ
.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

Vin vin 0 pwl(0 0 2u @VSUP@ 4u 0)
Xsch vin sout vdd 0 schmitt_hv

.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13
.tran 1n 4u

.control
run
* Trip point on the way UP: the input voltage when the (inverting) output
* first crosses mid-rail downward.  On the way DOWN: when it crosses back up.
meas tran t_up   when v(sout)=@VMID@ fall=1
meas tran t_dn   when v(sout)=@VMID@ rise=1
meas tran vth_up find v(vin) when v(sout)=@VMID@ fall=1
meas tran vth_dn find v(vin) when v(sout)=@VMID@ rise=1
print t_up t_dn vth_up vth_dn
.endc
.end
